      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FIRESIDE (10) settled close to the pace and kept finding but could only manage to finish second as the $1.75 favourite last start over 1800m in what was his first start at this track, that effort coming on the back of a sound second at Ballarat the run before. Draws out a little on the second line and may need luck at some point. Tackles a similar assignment and he can give this a mighty shake. CAPTAIN MOCKA (6) took full advantage of the inside draw when a dominant all of the way winner when on debut at this course and distance last start as the $1.70 favourite. Primary contender in a similar assignment. MY ULTIMATE BANJO (8) is also high on the list of contenders despite a tough draw. Best form measures up favourably in this line-up so just needs a bit of luck to go his way. RIVERGUM REGALIA (1) is worth some thought after her last-start sixth over 1800m at this track on November when having to race three-wide over the early stages and then racing outside the leader at the bell.",
